{"id":28,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield"],"text":"It climbs trees by hooking on with its sharp claws. Sandslash shares the berries it gathers, dropping them down to Sandshrew waiting below the tree."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"The drier the area Sandslash lives in, the harder and smoother the Pokémon’s spikes will feel when touched."},{"games":["Let’s Go, Eevee!","Let’s Go, Pikachu!","Yellow"],"text":"It is skilled at slashing enemies with its claws. If broken, they start to grow back in a day."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"Thanks to its thick claws, it’s good at climbing trees. There are plenty of Sandslash that park themselves in trees and go right to sleep."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"Its claws and horns often break off. The broken claws and horns can be used to carve plows for tilling farm fields."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"It uses its claws to climb trees and then curls its body into a spiny ball, ready to drop onto any prey that appears."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Although they are sharp, its claws and spikes often break off. They grow back the next day, so it is not bothered by the temporary loss."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Sandslash can roll up its body as if it were a ball covered with large spikes. In battle, this Pokémon will try to make the foe flinch by jabbing it with its spines. It then leaps at the stunned foe to tear wildly with its sharp claws."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Sandslash’s body is covered by tough spikes, which are hardened sections of its hide. Once a year, the old spikes fall out, to be replaced with new spikes that grow out from beneath the old ones."},{"games":["Y","LeafGreen","Blue","Red"],"text":"Curls up into a spiny ball when threatened. It can roll while curled up to attack or escape."},{"games":["X","SoulSilver","Silver"],"text":"If it digs at an incredible pace, it may snap off its spikes and claws. They grow back in a day."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"The spikes on its body are made up of its hardened hide. It rolls up and attacks foes with its spikes."},{"games":["White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It curls up, then rolls into foes with its back. Its sharp spines inflict severe damage."},{"games":["HeartGold","Gold"],"text":"In an attempt to hide itself, it will run around at top speed to kick up a blinding dust storm."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Sand Veil","hidden":false,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's evasiveness in a sandstorm."},{"name":"Sand Rush","hidden":true,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's Speed stat in a sandstorm."}],"eggGroups":["Field"],"genderRate":4,"hatchCounter":20,"baseHappiness":70,"growthRate":"medium","habitat":"rough terrain","color":"Yellow","shape":"Upright","evolution":{"id":27,"name":"Sandshrew","condition":null,"children":[{"id":28,"name":"Sandslash","condition":"Lv. 22 or Use Ice Stone","children":[]}]},"moves":{"game":"Scarlet / Violet","level":[[1,10],[1,28],[1,40],[1,111],[1,306],[9,205],[12,210],[15,229],[18,523],[21,129],[26,154],[31,328],[36,163],[41,91],[46,360],[51,14],[56,201],[61,89]],"machine":[332,97,133,34,280,523,174,91,38,529,414,89,283,203,263,206,374,411,264,416,441,360,667,63,282,141,67,232,341,189,398,182,156,157,317,328,201,815,421,214,479,191,446,707,444,164,241,162,129,14,36,851,168,675,404],"egg":[68,175,468,232,189,400],"tutor":[]},"cards":[{"id":"me1-69","name":"Sandslash","set":"Mega Evolution","date":"2025-09-26","rarity":"Common","number":"69","artist":null,"img":"me1/69"},{"id":"sv6-98","name":"Sandslash","set":"Twilight Masquerade","date":"2024-05-24","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"98","artist":"Nisota Niso","img":"sv6/98"},{"id":"sv3pt5-28","name":"Sandslash","set":"151","date":"2023-09-22","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"28","artist":"kodama","img":"sv3pt5/28"},{"id":"swsh8-132","name":"Sandslash","set":"Fusion Strike","date":"2021-11-12","rarity":"Uncommon","number":"132","artist":"Kyoko Umemoto","img":"swsh8/132"},{"id":"sm12-138","name":"Alolan Sandsl